risk of ovarian carcinoma: a prospective study</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>2004</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>281</fpage><lpage>286</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Cancer||108|281||bib11|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Strom</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimmel</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Farrar</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Metz</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Brensinger</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Nessel</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Localio</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predictors of recall of over-the-counter and prescription non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug exposure</article-title><source>Pharmacoepidemiol Drug Saf</source><year>2006</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>39</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Pharmacoepidemiol Drug Saf||15|39||bib12|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meier</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Jick</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Association between acetaminophen or nonsteroidal antiinflammatory drugs and risk of developing ovarian, breast, or colon cancer</article-title><source>Pharmacotherapy</source><year>2002</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>309</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Pharmacotherapy||22|303||bib13|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moysich</surname><given-names